<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Besleney</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An eastern Circassian princely tribe on the upper Kuban and Laba, closely related to the Kabardians, whose descendants are the Cherkess of Karachay-Cherkessia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Besleney lived on the upper Kuban, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laba-river">Laba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urup">Urup</a> rivers, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-kabarda">Kabarda</a> and the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a>. Tradition links their princely house to the Kabardian aristocracy, and their speech is close to Kabardian. They appear as a distinct community from the 16th and 17th centuries; earlier history is not separately recorded.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Princes and nobles ruled over free peasants and serfs according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Adyghe</a> code of conduct. The Besleney were horse breeders and herders, and their princes alternately allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-kabarda">Kabarda</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crimean-khanate">Crimean Khanate</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Their position on the routes between east and west <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/circassia">Circassia</a> gave them influence beyond their size.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> brought them under its control in the course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-circassian-war">Russo-Circassian War</a>, completed in 1864. Many emigrated to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, but part remained, and their descendants form much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Cherkess</a> people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karachay-cherkessia">Karachay-Cherkessia</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-besleney.jpg" alt="Principality of Besleney" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Liptink0 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Principality_of_Besleney_1820s.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kabardian (Besleney dialect)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Besleney, Beslenei</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1682&amp;focus=principality-of-besleney" aria-label="Principality of Besleney on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5648 226 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Besleney lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5955 888h0M6487 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5968 482h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5968 482h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=1682&amp;focus=principality-of-besleney">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

